Z||000000||Philphine||01-03-2001||12:31 PM||||<BR>had to have it vet tested (hate the vet, with a passion i might add). the car gets put on rollers and one of the workers (i hate them driving my car too) runs it up to about 25mph while you sit outside the car in a booth. sounded pretty good. free flow cat with stock gt exhaust and two resonator tips. too bad it's just on a 4cyl though.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||01-03-2001||01:36 PM||||I snuck my way out of vet testing this year. The Formula was up for it, I stopped, waited in line for an hour(as usual) and I was the next car up for my lane. The computers went down, and they counldn't get to me. I was given a 30 day extension paper. I then went to the DMV to renew my registration. Since the lady never once looked up at me, I pulled out the extension paper and told her it was my e-chech certificate telling that the car had passed. She never even looked. She gave me my new tags, and it's been about 4 months since then. Saved me $20, and the anxiousness of having someone else drive my car on the rollers. Don't need it again for two years <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||01-03-2001||01:38 PM||||It seems that most Fieros have a nice exhaust note. When you add the GT crossflow exhaust it sounds sweet. It must be because the exhaust system has a short run. I have never heard a quiet Fiero. The louder & mellower the sound is the better. <P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||firstfiero||01-04-2001||09:26 AM||||        I think fiero's are one of the best sounding stock cars you can buy....still gives me goose bumps when I start her.  86 se||||reg||12
